From: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh <code@jzab.de>
Subject: [PATCH] [recovery-init] Switch dwc3-msm glue to peripheral when the
 UDC is missing

On some Qualcomm dwc3-msm devices the UDC named by
androidboot.usbcontroller (on Sony pdx246: a600000.dwc3) is only
registered after the glue device a600000.ssusb is switched to peripheral
mode. usb_setup_configfs() writes the mode through
/sys/class/udc/<udc>/device/.., which does not exist yet, so the gadget
never binds and there is no telnet in the recovery/debug initrd.

If the UDC is missing, wait up to 5 s for the glue's mode attribute
(androidboot.usb.dwc3_msm, or <address>.ssusb derived from the UDC
name), write "peripheral" to it and wait up to 5 s for the UDC. pdx246's
own recovery does the same (init.recovery.qcom.rc). Devices whose UDC
already exists are unaffected. Same change as hybris-boot 24dc2d0 (branch
hybris-23.2), plus the wait for the mode attribute.

Applies to mer-hybris/hybris-initrd 7b972b6 (recovery-init is identical
at ecb295c). droid-hal-img-boot-pdx246 ships the result as the override
initrd-pdx246/recovery-init; tools/check-initrd-overrides.sh checks that
the two agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 recovery-init | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/recovery-init b/recovery-init
index c7d9a9f..88c9ba1 100755
--- a/recovery-init
+++ b/recovery-init
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2025 Jolla Mobile Ltd
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2021 Open Mobile Platform LLC.
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2013-2015 Jolla Ltd.
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh
 #
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 #
@@ -67,6 +68,27 @@ usb_setup_configfs() {
             esac
         done
     fi
+    # pdx246: on Qualcomm dwc3-msm the UDC named by androidboot.usbcontroller
+    # (a600000.dwc3) is only registered once the glue device (a600000.ssusb)
+    # is switched to peripheral mode, as the device's own recovery does
+    # (init.recovery.qcom.rc). The write below goes through /sys/class/udc,
+    # which does not exist before that, so the gadget would never bind.
+    if [ -n "$udc" ] && [ ! -e /sys/class/udc/"$udc" ]; then
+        glue="$(get_opt androidboot.usb.dwc3_msm | head -1)"
+        [ -z "$glue" ] && glue="${udc%%.*}.ssusb"
+        i=0
+        while [ ! -e /sys/bus/platform/devices/"$glue"/mode ] && [ $i -lt 50 ]; do
+            sleep 0.1
+            i=$((i + 1))
+        done
+        write /sys/bus/platform/devices/"$glue"/mode peripheral
+        i=0
+        while [ ! -e /sys/class/udc/"$udc" ] && [ $i -lt 50 ]; do
+            sleep 0.1
+            i=$((i + 1))
+        done
+        log_kmsg "USB: $glue set to peripheral, UDC $udc $([ -e /sys/class/udc/"$udc" ] && echo present || echo missing)"
+    fi
     # Force peripheral mode by default
     write /sys/class/udc/"$udc"/device/../mode peripheral
     echo "$udc" > $GADGET_DIR/g1/UDC
